    "title": "Interview: Tom Izzo ahead of Michigan State's Sweet 16 matchup with UConn - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Kress ,\n8 hours ago\nEAST LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) – Michigan State is preparing for its 17th Sweet 16 appearance under head coach Tom Izzo.\nThe Spartans will be taking on UConn at 9:45 p.m. on Friday out in Washington D.C. The game will be on CBS.\nIzzo sat down this week with WLNS Sports Director Ian Kress to discuss making it to the second weekend of the NCAA Tournament and Friday’s game with the Huskies.\nThis will be the third time Michigan State and UConn have met in the tournament. In 2009, MSU beat the Huskies in the Final Four. In 2014, UConn beat the Spartans in the Elite Eight.\nLast week, the Spartans defeated North Dakota State, 92-67, in the first round of the NCAA Tournament on Thursday and then defeated Louisville, 77-69, in the second round on Saturday.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.",
    "summary": "EAST LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) – Michigan State is preparing for its 17th Sweet 16 appearance under head coach Tom Izzo. Izzo sat down this week with WLNS Sports Director Ian Kress to discuss making it to the second weekend of the NCAA Tournament and Friday’s game with the Huskies. This will be the third time Michigan State and UConn have met in the tournament. Last week, the Spartans defeated North Dakota State, 92-67, in the first round of the NCAA Tournament on Thursday and then defeated Louisville, 77-69, in the second round on Saturday.",
